==Drop Locations==
{{DropLocations}}

==Notes==
* This mod can be equipped on the following weapons:
**{{Weapon|Ogris}}
**{{Weapon|Penta}}
**{{Weapon|Secura Penta}}
**{{Weapon|Carmine Penta}}
**{{Weapon|Tenet Ferrox}}
**{{Weapon|Tenet Envoy}}
**{{Weapon|Tonkor}}
**{{Weapon|Torid}}
**{{Weapon|Zarr}}
**{{Weapon|Helstrum}}
*When equipped, this removes the grenade's immediate explosion; it will explode after the 'fuse' duration of '''4s''' ends.
*Does almost nothing for {{Weapon|Penta}} weapons:
**Normal grenades will stick but will '''not''' explode on their own after the 'fuse' duration ends.
**{{M|Tether Grenades}} are intangible and will '''not''' stick to enemies, normally sticking to surfaces even without {{M|Adhesive Blast}}.
**{{M|Napalm Grenades}} will stick and will explode once the 'fuse' duration ends, but can still be detonated manually.
*In {{ver|17.10}}, Adhesive Blast now gives 17% per rank and reaches 100% at full rank.
*As of {{ver|21.3.1}}, Adhesive Blast cannot be equipped on {{Weapon|Javlok}} nor {{Weapon|Scourge}}.

== Trivia == 
*Pre-{{Ver|19.10}}, with the exception of the {{Weapon|Zarr}} and {{Weapon|Javlok}}, Adhesive Blast possessed the ability to deal damage over time and proc [[Status Effect]]s, this was later revealed that the ability of stuck projectiles to deal a DoT was unintentional and was removed.
**Additionally, if Adhesive Blast was equipped upon a manually detonated projectile such as the {{Weapon|Penta}}'s grenades, the damage over time effect would apply indefinitely due to the grenades' lack of fuse time.
**During this time, although its description stated "and deal +60% extra damage", it reportedly never did.

